# THE SIFREI ROWS on Numbers 18:1-32 (THE NUMBERS WALK sitting 5 — KORACH, 2026-09-10): piskaot 116-122 by POSITION, 14 rows at the
# shelf's row grain, each opened and verdicted; the middah named where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md: I1 a-fortiori, I2 the
# identity of wording, I3 the paradigm / prototype, I4-I7 general-particular, I8 the exemplar departing from the general, I13 two
# verses reconciled by a third). The Sifrei has NO ROW on chapters 16-17 (asserted in korach_ink.py — the rebellion, the earth, the
# fire, the plague and the staffs read on Onkelos alone); every head of 116-122 sits in order, none mistyped.
from korach_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

# ---- piska 116 (18:1-7): the sin of the sanctuary and of the priesthood; the Levites joined; the two-way fence; the stranger ----
srow(116, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE THING RELEGATED TO AARON IS EXHORTED TO AARON; THE SIN OF THE SANCTUARY = THE PRIESTS\' MISHANDLED OFFERINGS; ELI\'S SONS AND JERUSALEM; THE SIN OF THE PRIESTHOOD = KEEPING STRANGERS OUT; THE LEVITES BEAR THEIR OWN SIN, NOT THE PRIESTS\'; "YOUR BROTHERS" EXCLUDES ISRAELITES AND WOMEN; "WITH YOU" = THE LEVITES\' SONG; TREASURERS AND TRUSTEES; THE PRIESTS INSIDE, THE LEVITES OUTSIDE; THE ARK IS "THE HOLY"; BOTH THEY AND YOU — THE TWO-WAY FENCE; R. YEHOSHUA B. CHANANIA AND THE GATEKEEPER; REBBI\'S CENSUS OF THE DEMARCATION VERSES; "WHY REITERATE? BECAUSE KORACH CAME"; LEVITICAL SONG INTIMATED; THE WARNING AND THE PUNISHMENT; "NO MORE WRATH" — FOUR "NO MORE"S EACH PAID BY A PRIOR EVENT. "And the LORD said to Aaron" (18:1): R. Yishmael — what is relegated to Aaron is exhorted to Aaron; R. Yoshiyah — "bear the sin of the sanctuary": a priest who sprinkled blood or burned fat not knowing in whose name; R. Yonathan — one who took the flesh before the sprinkling or the breast and thigh before the fats (Lev 7:7, 7:31): Eli\'s decree sealed for the abuse of offerings (1 Sam 2:15-17 — and 2:17\'s "the men SCORNED the offering of the LORD" is chapter 16\'s own scorn-verb and offering-word: computed in the ledger\'s ink section) and Jerusalem\'s (Ezek 22:8 "you despised My holy things"); "the sin of your priesthood" — what is relegated to the priesthood (keeping strangers out), not to the court (18:7 already speaks of the court\'s charge); "you and your sons" — not Israelites; the Levites too? "and they shall bear THEIR sin" (18:23) — their own, not the priests\'; "your brothers" — "the tribe of Levi" excludes Israelites, "brothers" excludes women; R. AKIVA: "with you" here and "with you" at 18:7 (I2) — the Levites exhorted against defect in their SONG at their stand; "they shall serve you" — treasurers and trustees from among them, not the priestly service ("they shall keep your charge", 18:3; and 18:6 "given to the LORD, not to the priests" decides); "before the tent of testimony" — priests within, Levites without (18:4 deciding); "the holy" (18:3) is THE ARK (4:20); "and to the altar" the altar\'s service; "they shall not come near" the warning, "and they shall not die" the punishment; whence priests punished for the Levites\' service? "both they and you" — and R. YEHOSHUA B. CHANANIA to R. Yochanan b. Gudgada: "get back, you are close to forfeiting your life — I am of the gatekeepers and you of the singers" (the fence enacted on the page); REBBI: "both they and you" not needed — the Kohathites\' 4:18-19, Gershon and Merari\'s 4:19, the priests barred from dismantling by 1:51 "and the stranger that draws near shall die", and one Levite service to another by 3:38 — "then why \'both they and you\'? BECAUSE KORACH CAME AND CONTESTED AARON\'S PREROGATIVE, SCRIPTURE REITERATED THE ENTIRE EXHORTATION" (the chapter\'s law read as the rebellion\'s consequence — the juxtaposition the ink\'s own order carries); variantly "both they and you" = as you at the altar, so they; R. NATHAN: Levitical SONG intimated here, explicated by Ezra; Chanania: from "God answered him by VOICE" (Exod 19:19); "and a stranger shall not draw near to you" (18:4) — THE WARNING, 18:7\'s "shall be put to death" THE PUNISHMENT; "you shall keep the charge of the sanctuary and of the altar" (18:5) — a warning to a court of Israelites to exhort the priests, the service properly done fending off calamity; "SO THAT THERE BE NO MORE WRATH" — why "no more"? He had already vented it (17:11); likewise "no more a flood" (Gen 9:11), "no more to the goat-demons" (Lev 17:7 — the export\'s "18:7" a slip), "the children of Israel shall no more draw near" (18:22 — because they had, at 16:35): FOUR "NO MORE"S EACH PAID BY A PRIOR EVENT — a lexical rule on the adverb, and the ink confirms the first: 18:5 is 1:53\'s clause with ONE WORD ADDED, "more" (computed). The exam: Zevachim 2 (the wrong-name sprinkling); Mishnah Middot 1 (the watches); Arakhin 11a-b (the song); Sanhedrin 81b, 83a (the stranger\'s death).')
srow(116, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'GIVEN TO THE LORD, NOT TO THE PRIESTS; THE GENEALOGY CHAMBER BEHIND THE VEIL; SERVICE BY LOT AS THE BLOOD IS BY LOT; A SERVICE OF GIFT = EATING IN THE PROVINCES EQUATED WITH THE TEMPLE\'S SERVICE (R. TARFON TO R. GAMLIEL); THE WASHING OF THE HANDS SCRIPTURAL; THE STRANGER PUT TO DEATH ONLY FOR A SERVICE, EVEN IN PURITY; AT THE HANDS OF HEAVEN (YISHMAEL) OR BY STRANGULATION (AKIVA) — THE FORK ON "SHALL BE PUT TO DEATH". "And I, behold, I have taken your brothers... given to the LORD" (18:6) — to the LORD, not to the priests; "you and your sons shall guard your priesthood for every thing of the altar" (18:7) — R. Eliezer HaKappar: whatever pertains to the altar is yours alone; "and within the veil" — the chamber behind the holy of holies where priestly genealogy was ascertained (Mishnah Middot 5:4\'s room named on the clause); "and you shall serve" — not in concert: "a service of MATANAH (gift)": as the application of the blood is BY LOT, so all services by lot (I2 on the gift-word — the lots of Mishnah Yoma 2 and Tamid derived here); "AS A SERVICE OF GIFT HAVE I GIVEN YOUR PRIESTHOOD" — the eating of holy things in the provinces (terumah outside the Temple) EQUATED with the Temple\'s service in the Temple: R. TARFON late to the study house — "I was serving"; R. Gamliel: "is there service now?"; R. Tarfon: this verse (the priesthood\'s eating a service after the destruction — the tradition\'s own scene on the clause); REBBI: as the Temple service washes the hands first, so the eating in the provinces — hands, not hands and feet (the place decides): THE WASHING OF HANDS SCRIPTURALLY PRESCRIBED from this clause (Chullin 106a\'s derivation); "the stranger that draws near shall be put to death" — TO THE SERVICE, not for entering: an a-fortiori from the blemished priest (warned only for a service) to the stranger (I1); EVEN IN PURITY — an a-fortiori from the unclean enterer (Num 19:13) to the unclean server; R. YISHMAEL: "shall be put to death" here and "shall die" at 17:28 (I2) — AT THE HANDS OF HEAVEN; R. AKIVA: "shall be put to death" here and the false prophet\'s (Deut 13:6) — BY STRANGULATION: THE DEATH-MODE FORK on the stranger\'s "put to death", both arms by the identity of wording, each choosing its second seat (the answer sheet\'s Sanhedrin 81b, 84a carries both); the warning from "a stranger shall not draw near" (18:4 — the export cites "Devarim 18:4", a slip for Bamidbar). The exam: Sanhedrin 81b-84a (the stranger\'s mode); Yoma 2 (the lots); Chullin 106a (the hands); Zevachim 15b-17a (the stranger\'s service).')
# ---- piska 117 (18:8-14): the twenty-four gifts' covenant; the sanctuary's, the wave-offerings', the border's; the devotions ----
srow(117, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"THE LORD SPOKE TO AARON" — THROUGH MOSES, BY 17:5\'S "TO HIM"; "AND I, BEHOLD" = WITH JOY; THE FLOOD\'S "AND I, BEHOLD" ANSWERED; R. NATHAN\'S "AND I — WILLINGLY; BEHOLD — WITH JOY" FROM EXOD 4:14. "And the LORD spoke to Aaron" (18:8): I would think to Aaron; but 17:5 "as the LORD spoke to Moses ABOUT HIM" — the speaking was TO MOSES, to tell Aaron (the frame\'s address read through the chapter before: THE INK\'S OWN COUNT — the LORD addresses Aaron alone at five Torah seats, three in this chapter, computed in the ledger); "And I, behold" — with JOY (the twenty-four gifts): R. Yishmael, whose disciples object from the flood\'s "And I, behold, I bring the flood" (Gen 6:17) — a joy? "when His angerers are lost from the world it is a joy to Him" (Prov 11:10; Ps 3:9-10, 10:16, 104:35); R. NATHAN: "and I" — willingly, "behold" — with joy, from "BEHOLD, he goes out to meet you... and will REJOICE in his heart" (Exod 4:14 — Aaron\'s own joy at Moses\' return, the joy-word\'s proof-seat computed in the ledger). The middah: the lexical rule on "behold" (E-class, the particle read); the address resolved by a prior verse (I13\'s form).')
srow(117, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'THE COVENANT WRITTEN, SEALED AND RECORDED BECAUSE KORACH CONTESTED — THE JUXTAPOSITION\'S REASON; "IN YOUR MERIT"; "FOR ANOINTING" = GREATNESS (OR ANOINTMENT, R. YITZCHAK); THE MOST HOLY FROM THE FIRE = THE BURNT-OFFERING\'S HIDE; THE FOUR LISTS; "WHICH THEY RETURN" = THE PROSELYTE\'S THEFT; THE LEPER\'S LOG; EATEN WITHIN THE CURTAINS, BY MALES, IN HOLINESS EVEN WHAT IS UNFIT TO EAT; THE LOWER-ORDER OFFERINGS AND THE BORDER GIFTS INCLUDED; THE FIVE BORDER TERMS; BIKKURIM HOLY WHILE ATTACHED; "EVERY CLEAN ONE OF YOUR HOUSEHOLD" TWICE = THE BETROTHED DAUGHTER OF AN ISRAELITE; THE TOSHAV AND THE SACHIR; R. YOCHANAN B. BAG BAG\'S A-FORTIORI AND THE SAGES\' RULE. "For all the hallowed things" (18:8): Scripture forged a covenant with Aaron with the holy of holies — WHY? "for Korach arose and contested the priesthood": A KING gave a retainer a field WITHOUT writing, sealing or recording; someone contested it; the king: "let anyone come and contest — now I write, seal and record it" — WHEREFORE THIS SECTION IS JUXTAPOSED WITH KORACH (the tradition\'s own reason for the chapter\'s place — the map of chapters 16-18 as one causal run: E-class adjacency read as a deed\'s registration); "to you have I given them" — in your merit; "lemashchah" — GREATNESS (Lev 7:35\'s "mishchat Aaron"), or R. Yitzchak: anointment (Ps 133:2\'s oil on Aaron\'s beard) — a fork on one word (the translation takes GREATNESS: Onkelos 18:8, cut in the ledger); "to your sons" — in their merit; "an everlasting statute" — all generations; "this shall be yours from the holy of holies, from the fire" (18:9) — what remains of a thing wholly consigned to fire? only THE BURNT-OFFERING\'S HIDE (the census of the fire-consumed); "all their offerings" — the two loaves and the showbread; "all their meal-offerings" — the sinner\'s and the donative; "all their sin-offerings" — the individual\'s and the communal (Lev 6:18), the bird\'s and the beast\'s; "all their guilt-offerings" — the certain, the suspended, the nazirite\'s, the leper\'s (four verdict lists on four nouns); "which they shall return to Me" — THE PROSELYTE\'S THEFT reverting to the priests (5:8 — sitting 2\'s unit num_05_camp_pure_theft, the pointer); "holy of holies" — the leper\'s log of oil; "in the holy of holies shall you eat it" (18:10) — within the curtains, in the court; R. YEHUDAH: if gentiles surrounded the court, eaten even in the sanctuary; "every male" — males of the priesthood; "holy shall it be to you" — even what is unfit to eat is eaten in holiness; "the terumah of their gift" (18:11) — the LOWER-ORDER offerings included in the covenant as the most holy were; "from all the wave-offerings" — requires waving; "to your daughters" — the covenant for the generations; "every clean one" — eaten by the clean; "all the best of the oil" (18:12) — the BORDER gifts included too: "the best of the oil" = terumah gedolah (Deut 18:4), "all the best" = terumat ma\'aser (18:26), "the first of them" = the first shearing (Deut 18:4), "which they give" = shoulder, cheeks and maw (Deut 18:3), "to the LORD" = CHALLAH (15:20 — sitting 4\'s pointer answered here in the Sifrei\'s own map: five border terms on five clauses); "the first-fruits of all that is in their land" (18:13) — holiness takes on BIKKURIM WHILE ATTACHED to the ground (against terumah — the a-fortiori refused by the clause, I1); "to you have I given them" (18:12) — to the priest; "every clean one of your HOUSEHOLD" (18:13) after "in your HOUSE" (18:11) — the repetition INCLUDES THE DAUGHTER OF AN ISRAELITE BETROTHED TO A PRIEST as eating terumah (the ink: the clause twice, computed); the toshav and the sachir excluded by Lev 22:10 whether or not in your domain (I13); R. YOCHANAN B. BAG BAG to R. Yehudah in Netzivim: the betrothed eats terumah — R. Yehudah: "I held you expert... can you not expound a kal vachomer? if a Canaanite maidservant\'s money causes her to eat terumah (Lev 22:11), how much more the daughter of an Israelite whose intercourse acquires her — BUT WHAT CAN I DO? THE SAGES SAID: she does not eat until she enters the chuppah; once entered, even without intercourse, she eats, and if she dies her husband inherits" — AN A-FORTIORI OVERRIDDEN BY A DECREE ON THE RECORD (Mishnah Ketubot 5:2-3\'s rows with their reason; the middah stated and set aside — MIDDOT.md governance). The exam: Mishnah Zevachim 5, Menachot; Ketubot 5:2-3, 57b-58a; Yevamot 66a-68a; Bikkurim 1; Kiddushin 1:1 (the maidservant).')
srow(117, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'EVERY DEVOTED THING IN ISRAEL — GENTILES\', WOMEN\'S AND BONDSMEN\'S TOO; THE FOUR-WAY DISPUTE ON UNQUALIFIED DEVOTIONS. "Every devoted thing in Israel shall be yours" (18:14): the devotions of gentiles, women and bondsmen included ("in Israel" read wide); R. YOSSI HAGELILI: unqualified devotions to the PRIESTS (Lev 27:21 "as a devoted field, to the priest"); even if specified "for Temple maintenance"? no — Lev 27:28 "every devoted thing is most holy to the LORD" (the specified case); R. YEHUDAH B. BETEIRA: unqualified to TEMPLE MAINTENANCE (27:28); even if specified "to the priests"? no — "ach" ("but") excludes; R. YEHUDAH B. BAVA: unqualified to the PRIESTS (18:14); even if "to the LORD"? no — 27:28; R. SHIMON: unqualified to HEAVEN (27:28); even if "to the priest"? no — 18:14: FOUR AUTHORITIES, ONE PAIR OF VERSES (Lev 27:21, 27:28 — both measured in the ledger), each reading the pair with the opposite default and the same exception — a DISPUTE row on the default of an unspecified devotion, Mishnah Arakhin 8:6\'s "unqualified devotions go to the priests" the answer sheet\'s row (the Lev 27 unit\'s valuation engine the callee). The middah: I4-I5 on "in Israel"; the dispute carried as a parameter (default_owner) for the compile.')
# ---- piska 118 (18:15-19): the firstborn — man, beast, the unclean, the redemption's money and time; the clean firstborn's blood, fat and flesh; the covenant of salt ----
srow(118, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'ALL THAT OPENS THE WOMB — "WHICH THEY OFFER" EXCLUDES THE UNCLEAN ANIMAL, "AND IN BEAST" RE-INCLUDES THE BLEMISHED; "IN MAN AND IN BEAST" — WHAT OBTAINS WITH THE MAN OBTAINS WITH HIS BEAST (THE LEVITES\' ASS EXEMPT); MAN AND BEAST LIKENED BOTH WAYS (THE MISCARRIAGE, THE PLACE OF GIVING, THE THIRTY DAYS); KEREM BEYAVNEH — R. TARFON ON "REDEEM, YOU SHALL REDEEM"; THE ASS ALONE REDEEMED, AND WITH A SHEEP (EXOD 13:13, 34:20 TWICE); "THE UNCLEAN BEAST YOU SHALL REDEEM" REASSIGNED TO TEMPLE-DEDICATIONS; IMMEDIATELY (THE ASS) OR AFTER A MONTH (THE MAN); GENERAL-PARTICULAR-GENERAL ON THE REDEMPTION MONEY — MOVABLE PROPERTY, NOT BONDSMEN, WRITS OR LAND (REBBI: WRITS ONLY); "TWENTY GERAH IT SHALL BE" — MORE, NOT LESS; "OX, SHEEP, GOAT" — NO HYBRID; "THEY ARE CONSECRATED" — THE TITHE AND THE PASCHAL LAMB TAKE ONE SPILLING (YOSHIYAH), OR THE FATS (YITZCHAK), ABBA CHANAN\'S A-FORTIORI; ONE APPLICATION OF BLOOD — THE A-FORTIORI, ITS CONVERSE, THE REFUTATION, THE RETURN; THE FATS = THE PEELABLE LAYER; "AS THE WAVE-BREAST" — FIRST-BORN EATEN TWO DAYS AND A NIGHT: KEREM BEYAVNEH AGAIN (TARFON, YOSSI HAGELILI, AKIVA, YISHMAEL, ELAZAR); "FOR YOU SHALL IT BE" = THE BLEMISHED FIRSTBORN TO THE PRIEST; THE SECTION GENERAL AT BOTH ENDS AND PARTICULAR IN THE MIDDLE; THE COVENANT OF SALT — WHAT PRESERVES. "All that opens the womb of all flesh" (18:15): "which they offer" excludes the unclean animal (not offered); "in beast" re-includes the blemished (the unclean would be out with it — I4-I5); "in man AND in beast" — the Levites\' ass exempt as the Levites\' sons are (3:12\'s exchange the ground); man likened to beast and beast to man (I3 both ways): the miscarriage exempt for both, the redemption given to a priest WHEREVER (against Deut 12:6\'s bringing to the Temple — I13), the thirty days for both (18:16); "REDEEM, YOU SHALL REDEEM" — asked in KEREM BEYAVNEH: a firstborn beast that died, redeemed and fed to dogs? R. TARFON: you redeem the unclean, never the clean, alive or dead (the doubled infinitive read as scope, on its one seat); "the firstborn of the unclean beast you shall redeem" — all unclean beasts? Exod 13:13 "the firstling of an ASS you shall redeem with a sheep" — the ass alone; the others with clothing and vessels? Exod 34:20 REPEATS it — the ass alone, and with a sheep (the repetition as a second exclusion — the ink\'s two seats measured in the ledger); then 18:15\'s "unclean beast" = a beast dedicated to Temple maintenance, redeemed by Lev 27:27 (the clause reassigned to keep it from being idle); "you shall redeem" — IMMEDIATELY, against 18:16\'s "from a month" for the man: the ass at once or any time, the man after thirty days with five shekels (Mishnah Bekhorot 1:4-7\'s rows); "and his redemption, from a month" — money or its value? "his redemption" GENERAL, "money, five shekels" PARTICULAR, "you shall redeem" GENERAL — I6, the general-particular-general: LIKE THE PARTICULAR, movable and worth money — whence: redeemed with anything EXCEPT bondsmen, writs and land; REBBI: except writs (Mishnah Bekhorot 8:8 with its derivation); "twenty gerah IT SHALL BE" — Lev 27:25 already fixes it: "it shall be" — he may INCREASE, not decrease (the clause re-purposed for the direction of deviation — a parameter with a floor); "the firstborn of an OX... a SHEEP... a GOAT" (18:17) — each must look its kind: no hybrid, no lookalike (Mishnah Bekhorot 1:5\'s rows); "you shall not redeem" — if he redeemed? "they are consecrated" — R. YOSHIYAH: the clause includes the (beast-)TITHE and the PASCHAL LAMB as requiring ONE SPILLING of blood, spelled out nowhere else; R. YITZCHAK: Deut 12:27 gives the spilling — then the fats\' burning; ABBA CHANAN in R. Eliezer\'s name: the fats follow a-fortiori (offerings unlike in blood are alike in fats) — so "they are consecrated" gives the one spilling: THREE READINGS OF ONE CLAUSE, each assigning it the job the others\' verses leave open (a verdict table built by elimination — MIDDOT.md); "their blood you shall sprinkle" — ONE application: the a-fortiori (where fats increase, blood decreases — here fats decrease, so blood the more), ITS CONVERSE, the converse REFUTED by Lev 1:11\'s "roundabout" (two that are four), THE RETURN to the original — the full a-fortiori protocol run on the page (I1 with reversal and refutation: the form recorded); "their fats" — the peelable membraned layer, not the rib-cage fats (a-fortiori); "a fire-offering" — not accepted until consumed; "a sweet savor" — "My pleasure that I spoke and My will was done" (the standing gloss); "AND THEIR FLESH SHALL BE FOR YOU AS THE WAVE-BREAST" (18:18) — first-born likened to the breast and thigh of PEACE-OFFERINGS: eaten TWO DAYS AND A NIGHT — KEREM BEYAVNEH: R. TARFON says two days and a night; the new disciple R. YOSSI HAGELILI: "how do you know?" — Tarfon: both are holy things; Yossi: both are gifts to the priest, so like the SIN-OFFERING, one day and a night; Tarfon: lower-order from lower-order, not from most holy; Yossi: gift-to-priest from gift-to-priest; TARFON SILENT; R. AKIVA: the verse likens it to the peace-offerings\' breast; Yossi: I liken it to the THANK-OFFERING\'S breast (one day); AKIVA: "for you shall it be" ADDS a second "being" — a second day; R. YISHMAEL: the thank-offering\'s breast is itself derived from the peace-offering — you would learn from what is itself learned? not so: two days and a night, and "for you shall it be" = THE BLEMISHED FIRSTBORN reverts to the priest (spelled out nowhere else); R. ELAZAR: from Deut 15:20\'s "year in year" — the last day of one year and the first of the next (a calendar reading of the span) — THE ANALOGY\'S TARGET CONTESTED (peace- or thank-offering) and settled by a redundant clause: a middah-governance row (I3\'s choice of paradigm decided by the ink\'s extra word; the "learned from the learned" bar — MIDDOT.md); "all the terumah of the holy things" (18:19) — sections general-then-particular, particular-then-general, and THIS ONE GENERAL AT BOTH ENDS (18:8, 18:19) AND PARTICULAR IN THE MIDDLE (I7\'s form named on the section\'s shape); "an everlasting statute" — the generations; "a covenant of salt forever" — a covenant with what PRESERVES and preserves others (the ink: the phrase\'s two seats, Aaron\'s and David\'s — computed). The exam: Mishnah Bekhorot 1 (the ass), 4 (the time), 8:8 (the money); Zevachim 5:8 (the firstborn\'s one application, two days and a night); Temurah 1; Bekhorot 12b-13a, 49b-51b (the five shekels and the sela); Zevachim 37a-b (the one spilling).')
# ---- piska 119 (18:20-25): no inheritance — the priests, the Levites, the others excluded; the twenty-four gifts; the crowns; the covenant of the Levites; the tithe as inheritance ----
srow(119, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'IN THEIR LAND YOU SHALL NOT INHERIT — THE EXCLUSIONS FROM 26:53\'S APPORTIONMENT: PRIESTS (18:20), LEVITES (18:23), BONDSMEN AND PROSELYTES (26:55), TUMTUM AND ANDROGYNOUS (26:54); NO PORTION OF THE SPOILS; "AT MY TABLE YOU EAT"; THE TWENTY-FOUR GIFTS, TWELVE IN THE SANCTUARY. "And the LORD said to Aaron: in their land you shall not inherit" (18:20): 26:53 "to these shall the land be apportioned" would include all — priests, Levites, Israelites, proselytes, women, bondsmen, those of uncertain sex, hermaphrodites; 18:20 EXCLUDES THE PRIESTS, 18:23 THE LEVITES, 26:55 "by the names of the tribes of their fathers" bondsmen and proselytes, 26:54 "a man according to his numbers" the two uncertain (a set carved by four clauses — the inheritance engine\'s exclusion table, the Zelophehad unit\'s callee; I4-I5); "in their land you shall not inherit" — the land\'s division; "no portion in their midst" — the SPOILS; "I am your portion and your inheritance" — AT MY TABLE you eat and drink (the king who gave all his sons gifts but one: "my son, at my table you eat" — Lev 6:10, Deut 18:1); TWENTY-FOUR PRIESTLY GIFTS, twelve in the sanctuary: the sin-offering, the guilt-offering, the leper\'s log remnant, the omer\'s remnant, the two loaves, the showbread, the meal-offerings\' remnant, the thank-offering\'s terumah (Lev 7:14), the breast and thigh, the nazirite\'s ram\'s shoulder (ten named of the twelve — the export\'s list; the answer sheet Bava Kamma 110b, Chullin 133b carry the twenty-four). The middah: I4-I5 by four clauses; the twenty-four a data list.')
srow(119, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'TWELVE IN THE BORDERS; THE DAY OF THE COVENANT A DAY OF JOY; "MY COW\'S LEG WAS BROKEN FOR MY GOOD" — KORACH CAME FOR AARON\'S GOOD; JACOB SHOWN THE TEMPLE ON THE LADDER; ISRAEL EPITOMIZED AS PRIESTS, PRIESTS AS ANGELS — IF TORAH GOES FORTH FROM HIS MOUTH; DAVID ASKED ONLY FOR TORAH. Twelve in the borders: terumah, terumat ma\'aser, challah, bikkurim, the first shearing, the gifts (shoulder, cheeks, maw), the firstborn of man and of a clean beast, the firstling of an ass, devotions, the field of holding, the proselyte\'s theft (5:8) — ALL TWENTY-FOUR GIVEN TO THE PRIESTS "aside from terumah-related debts"; the covenant\'s day a day of great joy; R. YISHMAEL: as the folk-proverb, "my cow\'s leg was broken for my good" — FOR AARON\'S GOOD DID KORACH COME AND CONTEST (the retainer and the king again — the section juxtaposed with Korach: the chapter\'s cause stated a second time, now as Aaron\'s gain); R. ELAZAR HAKAPPAR: Jacob shown the Temple built and the priests officiating in the LADDER (Gen 28:12-13 — the ladder the Temple, its top the offerings\' scent, the angels the priests on the ramp, "the LORD standing on it" Amos 9:1\'s altar — the Bethel unit\'s dream read as the priesthood\'s preview); Israel epitomized as PRIESTS (Isa 61:6), priests as MINISTERING ANGELS (Mal 2:7) — "if Torah goes forth from his mouth; if not, like a beast that does not know its Creator"; beloved is Torah — David asked only for Torah (Ps 119:68, 117, 46, 54; 56:1; 119:109). CONTEXT-grade aggadah on a law seat, verdicted MATERIAL for the twenty-four\'s second list (the data list completed) and the juxtaposition\'s second statement.')
srow(119, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'DAVID GROWN GREAT IN TORAH: "how precious are Your loved ones" (Ps 139:17), "better to me is the Torah of Your mouth than thousands of gold and silver" (119:72) — gold and silver take a man out of both worlds, Torah brings him to the world to come. Aggadah, no operator.')
srow(119, 4, 'MATERIAL', 'THE THREE CROWNS — TORAH, PRIESTHOOD, KINGDOM: AARON TOOK THE SECOND, DAVID THE THIRD, THE FIRST LEFT VACANT FOR ALL; "WHO IS GREATER, THE CROWNER OR THE KING?"; "THROUGH ME KINGS REIGN"; "THIS IS ALL OF MAN". "This is the Torah of man" (2 Sam 7:19): THREE CROWNS — the crown of Torah, of priesthood, of kingdom; Aaron merited and took the priesthood\'s, David the kingdom\'s, the Torah\'s left vacant that none say "had it been vacant I would have taken it" — whoever merits it is accounted as if all three were his; R. SHIMON B. ELAZAR: who is greater, the crowner or the king? the maker of officers or the officers? — both crowns come through Torah\'s power (Prov 8:15-16); "the end of the matter... for this is all of man" (Eccl 12:13). The tradition\'s ranking of the three offices stated on Aaron\'s covenant — Mishnah Avot 4:13\'s three crowns (with the fourth, the good name) the answer sheet\'s row; the priesthood\'s crown the chapter\'s subject (the dispute of Korach was over this crown — E-class, the section\'s theme named).')
srow(119, 5, 'MATERIAL', 'AARON\'S COVENANT GREATER THAN DAVID\'S — FOR THE WICKED SONS TOO; THE LEVITES\' COVENANT FORGED LIKE THE PRIESTS\', AT SINAI, WITH JOY; "IN EXCHANGE FOR THEIR SERVICE" — ACQUIRED BY THE LORD (YOSHIYAH) OR BY THE LAND (YONATHAN); THE TITHE AN INHERITANCE — DOES NOT CHANGE ITS PLACE; IF HE SERVES HE TAKES; "SHALL NO MORE DRAW NEAR" THE WARNING, "TO BEAR SIN, TO DIE" THE PUNISHMENT; "THE LEVITE — HE" = PERFORCE, AND IN SABBATICAL AND JUBILEE YEARS, AND NO PRIEST IN HIS STEAD (R. NATHAN\'S A-FORTIORI REFUSED); THE LEVITES BEAR THEIR OWN SIN; THE TITHE CALLED TERUMAH — MAY BE MADE TERUMAH FOR OTHER PRODUCE; "AS AN INHERITANCE" — EVEN WITHOUT THE TEMPLE; "THEREFORE I HAVE SAID" — NOT AFTER THE APPORTIONMENT EITHER, NOR IN THE KENITE\'S LAND, AND A WARNING TO THE COURT. GREATER IS THE COVENANT WITH AARON THAN WITH DAVID: Aaron merited for his sons whether righteous or wicked, David only for the righteous (Ps 132:12 "if your children keep My covenant") — THE INK\'S OWN SHARED PHRASE: "a covenant of salt" at Aaron\'s 18:19 and at David\'s 2 Chr 13:5 alone in the Bible (computed in the ledger) — the two covenants the Sifrei ranks are the two the ink names with one word; "a covenant of salt... and to the sons of Levi" (18:19-21) — the Levites\' covenant forged LIKE the priests\' (adjacency), stated at Sinai like it, with JOY like it ("behold" — Exod 4:14 again); "in exchange for their service" — R. YOSHIYAH: the priestly gifts acquired BY THE LORD and given to the priests, the Levites\' in exchange for the tent\'s service; R. YONATHAN: acquired BY THE LAND (Lev 27:30 "all the tithe of the land... is the LORD\'s") — a fork on the tithe\'s title; "all the tithe of Israel as an INHERITANCE" — as an inheritance does not change its place, first tithe does not (unlike second tithe → poor-tithe in the third and sixth years: the tithe engine\'s year-switch by contrast); "in exchange for the service" — IF HE SERVES HE TAKES (18:31\'s "wage" the same rule at 122:1); "the children of Israel shall no more draw near" (18:22) — the warning; "to bear sin, to die" — the punishment AT THE HANDS OF HEAVEN; "and the Levite, HE shall serve" (18:23) — why? "in exchange" might mean optional: HE — perforce; variantly: only in tithe-years? in SABBATICAL AND JUBILEE years too; R. NATHAN: no Levite there — may a priest serve? the a-fortiori (where Levites are unfit priests are fit — where Levites are fit, priests the more) REFUSED by "the Levite, HE" (I1 capped by the pronoun — Arakhin 11b); "they shall bear their sin" — the Levites\' own, not the Israelites\' nor the priests\' who enter where they should not (116:1\'s counterpart); "and in the midst of the children of Israel they shall not inherit" (18:23) — 26:53\'s apportionment excludes the Levites; "the tithe... which they set apart as TERUMAH" (18:24) — called terumah UNTIL terumat ma\'aser is separated: he may make it terumah for other untithed produce (a status rule read off a noun); "as an inheritance" — even when the Temple does not exist (the tithe outlives the service it pays for); "THEREFORE I HAVE SAID" (18:24) — after 18:23 already said it? not only at the apportionment but after it (no tribe carves the Levites a parcel); variantly: the Kenite, Kenizzite and Kadmonite lands (Gen 15:19, absent from Deut 7:1\'s seven) — no inheritance there either, forever; variantly: a warning to the court. The exam: Mishnah Ma\'aser Sheni 5; Arakhin 11b (the Levite\'s song and the priest); Chullin 131a-b (the tithe after the Temple); Yevamot 86a-b (the Levites\' tithe).')
# ---- piska 120-122 (18:26-32): the tithe of the tithe — from it, kind for kind; reckoned as the floor's grain; the Levites and the priests tithe too; the best; in every place; the wage; the warning ----
srow(120, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE TITHE IS OF THE PRODUCE, NOT OF THE LAND; "FROM IT" — KIND FOR ITS KIND, ROOTED FOR ROOTED, NEW FOR NEW; NOT ACROSS THE LAND\'S BORDER (LEV 27:30); "FROM IT" MUFNEH FOR THE MOURNER — THE TITHE AND THE PASCHAL LAMB. "And to the Levites shall you speak" (18:26): why? to teach that 18:21\'s "all the tithe" is ONE-TENTH OF THE PRODUCE, not of the land itself — "that I have given to you from them in their inheritance": no portion in the land, so a tenth of its produce (the ink\'s "from them" the ground — the compile\'s arithmetic on the produce); "then you shall separate from it" — from one kind for its kind, not for another; not from the rooted for the unrooted nor the reverse; not from the new crop for the old nor the old for the new (Mishnah Terumot 1:5\'s rows on "from it"); not from the land\'s produce for produce outside it nor the reverse — Lev 27:30 "all the tithe of THE LAND"; variantly, "FROM IT" is MUFNEH (free for a gezerah shavah — the shared-word analogy licensed by an "extra" word, I2\'s own condition stated): "from it" here and "(do not eat) from it" at the Paschal lamb (Exod 12:9) — as the tithe is forbidden to a mourner (Deut 26:14), so the Paschal lamb (the analogy runs FROM the tithe TO the lamb — the licensed direction recorded; the exam\'s Pesachim 36a, Yevamot 73b-74a). The middah: I2 by a mufneh word (the license named on the page — MIDDOT.md); the separation rules as data.')
srow(121, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"ACCOUNTED AS CORN FROM THE THRESHING FLOOR" — ONLY IF TAKEN AS PRESCRIBED (YISHMAEL); TERUMAT MA\'ASER LIKENED TO TERUMAH GEDOLAH AND THE LIKENESS RETURNING — BOTH OBLIGATORY; BY ESTIMATE AND BY THOUGHT (ABBA ELIEZER B. GOMEL); FROM WHAT IS PROCESSED — THE PILE EVENED, THE WINE SKIMMED, THE OIL DRIPPED; "SO YOU TOO" — THE PRIESTS SEPARATE TOO (OR THE LEVITES FROM THEIR OWN — YISHMAEL\'S A-FORTIORI FROM CHALLAH); "FROM ALL YOUR GIFTS" — THE TITHE OBTAINS WITH ALL PRODUCE, AND TERUMAH THE MORE (THREE A-FORTIORIS, ISSI B. MENACHEM\'S THIRD); "TO AARON" = TO A SCHOLAR; "FROM ALL ITS BEST, ITS HALLOWED PART" — TERUMAH GEDOLAH; DEUT 18:4 OBLIGATORY FROM "SHALL YOU SEPARATE"; NEUTRALIZED IN A HUNDRED AND ONE — AND THE TRANSLATOR STOPS. "And your terumah will be accounted for you as corn from the threshing floor" (18:27): R. YISHMAEL — when taken as prescribed (kind for kind, new for new); otherwise not accounted; variantly: terumat ma\'aser (the Levite\'s) likened to terumah gedolah (the Israelite\'s) — "it comes to teach and ends up learned": as terumat ma\'aser is OBLIGATORY, so terumah gedolah (the likeness read in both directions — I3\'s reciprocity named); ABBA ELIEZER B. GOMEL: as terumah gedolah may be taken BY ESTIMATE AND BY THOUGHT (without handling), so terumat ma\'aser (Mishnah Terumot 1:7, 4:6\'s rows; Bekhorot 58b-59a); "as corn from the threshing floor and the fullness of the pit" — not ears for grain, grapes for wine, olives for oil: FROM WHAT IS PROCESSED — whence: grain from when the pile is EVENED, wine from when it is SKIMMED, oil from when it has DRIPPED into the trough (Mishnah Ma\'aserot 1:6-7\'s thresholds on this clause — the tithe engine\'s "done" states); "thus shall YOU TOO separate" (18:28) — the priests give no tithe to the Levites, so might eat untithed? "you too": the priests separate terumah, tithe and terumat ma\'aser (which reverts to them); R. YISHMAEL: not needed — if CHALLAH, which does not obtain with all produce, obtains with the priests\' produce, the tithe which obtains with all the more (I1) — then "you too" = the LEVITES\' OWN tithe (their own produce) also subject; "from all your gifts" (18:29) — the tithe obtains with ALL produce, whence terumah the graver (death, Lev 22:9) the more (I1); variantly from second tithe (absent in the third and sixth years) to terumah; ISSI B. MENACHEM: from the tithe that comes only as an incentive to fear and learn (Deut 14:23) to the graver terumah — THREE A-FORTIORIS TO ONE VERDICT; "to Aaron the priest" — as Aaron was a CHAVER (a fellow, a scholar), priestly gifts only to a chaver (Chullin 130b); "from all your gifts... all the terumah of the LORD" — terumah gedolah, since 18:28 already spoke of terumat ma\'aser; Deut 18:4\'s "the first of your corn... shall you give" OBLIGATORY, from "shall you separate" (R. Yonathan — the export cites "11:29", a slip for 18:29); "from all its best, its hallowed part from it" — if it fell back in, it HALLOWS: terumah neutralized when one to a hundred (Mishnah Terumot 4:7\'s ratio derived from "its hallowed part FROM IT" — the data channel\'s number with its verse); clean terumah only? unclean too, a-fortiori — AND THE TRANSLATOR STOPS: "the translator has not been able to render meaningfully what follows until 122" — THE SHELF\'S OWN GAP, recorded (RESEARCH_LOG.md: the export\'s untranslated tail of piska 121). The exam: Mishnah Terumot 1, 4; Ma\'aserot 1; Bekhorot 58b-59a; Chullin 130b-131a; Yevamot 86a.')
srow(122, 1, 'MATERIAL', '"WHEN YOU SEPARATE ITS BEST" — A WARNING TO TAKE ONLY FROM THE CHOICEST; WHAT REMAINS IS COMMON, AS THE FLOOR\'S GRAIN AFTER TERUMAH; "IN EVERY PLACE" — EVEN A CEMETERY (THE A-FORTIORI FROM TERUMAH REFUSED); "YOU AND YOUR HOUSEHOLD" — THE ISRAELITE WIFE OF A LEVITE MAY DEPUTE THE SEPARATION; IF HE SERVES HE TAKES — A LEVITE WHO REFUSED ONE SERVICE HAS NO PORTION; "YOU SHALL NOT BEAR SIN" — ITS CONVERSE; "YOU SHALL NOT PROFANE, AND YOU SHALL NOT DIE" — THE WARNING TO LEVITES AND ISRAELITES BOTH. "When you separate its best part from it" (18:30): a warning to the Levites to take only from the CHOICEST (Onkelos "its beauty" — cut in the ledger); "reckoned to the Levites as the produce of the threshing floor" — since 18:24 called first tithe "terumah", might it keep terumah\'s holiness forever? as the floor\'s produce after terumah is CHULLIN (common), so first tithe after terumat ma\'aser is common (a status transition read off a likeness — the tithe engine\'s state change); "you may eat it in every place" (18:31) — EVEN IN A CEMETERY: the a-fortiori from terumah (both called "terumah", terumah eaten only in a clean place) REFUSED by the clause (I1 capped; the ink: "in every place" the Torah\'s other seat is Deut 12:13\'s ban on OFFERING in every place — computed); "you and your household" — an Israelite woman married to a Levite may DEPUTE the separation, not merely eat (the a-fortiori from the priest\'s wife eating the graver terumah settles the eating; the clause must add the deputing); "for it is your WAGE in exchange for your service" — IF HE SERVES HE TAKES; if not, not — whence: a Levite who took on every service but ONE has no portion in the Levitical dues (Mishnah Bekhorot 4:? / Arakhin 11b\'s rule: the whole service the condition); "you shall not bear sin because of it" (18:32) — if he did NOT separate the choicest, he DOES bear sin (the converse read); this tells of terumat ma\'aser — terumah gedolah too? "the holy things of the children of Israel you shall not profane, and you shall not die" — a warning to BOTH the Levites and the Israelites (the closing clause\'s two addressees; the ink: "and you shall not die" in the priests\' own words of Lev 8:35, 10:6-9 — computed). The exam: Mishnah Terumot 2:4-6 (the best), 4:3; Ma\'aser Sheni 5:6; Bekhorot 4; Arakhin 11b.')
